# local_enables
#
# This file controls which language-specific plugins and LazyVim extras
# are loaded. Most plugins are enabled by default; only language-specific
# features need to be explicitly enabled here.
#
# Format:
#   - One feature per line
#   - Lines starting with # are comments (with optional leading whitespace)
#   - Empty lines are ignored
#
# Setup: Copy this file to 'local_enables' (without the .default extension)
# and customize it for your machine.

# --- Language Support ---

# Uncomment the languages you want to enable on this machine:

# go
# typescript
# rust

# --- Custom Features ---
# You can define custom features and check them in plugin configs using:
#   enabled = require("config.local-features").is_enabled("your-feature")
